' ============================================================================
' PRODUCTION RUNTIME
' ============================================================================
|Production Runtime|

partition "Document Processing" {
  :Receive document\n(any format);

  :Stage 0 — Document Type Router;
  note right
    **Format detection + PDF sub-classification — <20ms CPU**

    PDF text layer quality validation heuristics:
    - Word recognition rate (real words vs character soup)
    - Character entropy (OCR garbage has unusual distribution)
    - Text/image layer overlap (scan+OCR both at same coords)

    PDF sub-types:
    - born_digital: text layer quality validated -> fast path
    - born_digital_degraded: poor OCR text -> image pipeline
    - scanned: no text layer -> image pipeline
    - hybrid: per-page routing

    **Outputs:**
    document_class, file_format, router_confidence,
    page_type_map (hybrid PDFs only)

    **Level 2 Detail:**
    production-runtime/prepare-doc-primary-workflow-detailed.puml

    **Source (planned):**
    - src/.../routing/document_type_router.py
  end note

  if (document_class?) then (native text OR\nvalidated born-digital PDF)
    :Pass to Unify directly\n(no image preprocessing);
    note right
      Fast path: DOCX, HTML, MD, LaTeX, CSV,
      XML, EPUB, VTT, validated born-digital PDF
      Saves ~55ms GPU per document
    end note
    stop
  else (image / scanned PDF /\nborn_digital_degraded /\nhybrid PDF pages)
  endif

  :Step 1 — Rasterization;
  note right
    PDFs only — images pass through

    Scanned PDF: use embedded DPI if >= 150 DPI,
    otherwise fallback to 300 DPI
    Hybrid PDF: per-page — born_digital pages -> fast path,
    scanned/image pages -> rasterize

    **Level 2 Detail:**
    production-runtime/prepare-doc-primary-workflow-high-level.puml

    **Source:**
    - src/.../ingestion/pdf_analyzer.py
    - src/.../ingestion/pdf_resolution.py
    - src/.../ingestion/pdf_upscaler.py
  end note

  :Step 1b — Lossless Conversion (PNG);
  note right
    Convert all inputs to PNG before any ML analysis.
    Eliminates JPEG block artifacts that corrupt:
    - MobileNetV4 orientation/skew detection
    - Character height estimation
    - SigLIP 2 IQA sharpness scoring
    PNG at 300 DPI letter page ~ 8-25 MB (acceptable)

    **Source:**
    - src/.../ingestion/format_normalizer.py
  end note

  :Step 2 — MobileNetV4-Conv-S\nPre-Correction Gate (~3ms GPU);
  note right
    **3 heads:**
    - Orientation (4-class: 0/90/180/270) + confidence score
    - Skew angle (regression +/- 10 deg)
    - Resolution quality (0-1 adequacy score)

    Confidence threshold: if orient_conf < 90%,
    skip rotation (better slightly skewed than wrong 90 deg)

    **Level 2 Detail:**
    model-training/prepare-doc-distillation.puml

    **Source:**
    - src/.../detection/iqa_ml.py
  end note

  :Step 3 — Geometric Corrections\n+ Border Removal;
  note right
    - Rotate to upright (if MobileNetV4 confident)
    - Deskew (if skew above threshold)
    - Border/scanner-bed crop
      (prevents layout analysis false positives)

    **Source:**
    - src/.../correction/corrections.py
  end note

  :Step 4 — Script-Aware\nAdaptive Resolution;
  note right
    Uses script class from Step 2 to select target:
    - Latin/Cyrillic/Greek:  32-48px (target ~40px)
    - CJK (Han/Kanji/Hangul): 40-60px (target ~50px)
    - Arabic/Hebrew:          28-42px (target ~35px)
    - Devanagari/Bengali:     36-52px (target ~44px)

    If char_height < script_min -> upscale
    Algorithm: Bicubic/Lanczos4 (never nearest-neighbor)
    Safety rails: 150-600 DPI equivalent, no downscaling

    **Source:**
    - src/.../ingestion/pdf_upscaler.py
  end note

  :Step 5 — Text Gate (<10ms);
  note right
    Fast ensemble heuristics on corrected + lossless image.
    Stroke density, CC analysis, edge density.
    Informs Layout Analysis routing (Step 6c).

    **Source:**
    - src/.../detection/text_gate.py

    **Documentation:**
    docs/api/detection.md
  end note

  if (blank page?) then (yes)
    :Record blank_page flag in metadata;
    note right
      Skip SigLIP 2 + Layout analysis.
      DQS = 0.0, routing = skip_ocr.
    end note
  else (has content)
    fork
      :Classical IQA\n(8 detectors);
      note left
        Measures ORIGINAL image quality
        (before quality corrections)
        Blur, noise, contrast, JPEG blockiness,
        illumination, binarization, bleed-through

        **Source:**
        src/.../detection/iqa_classical.py
      end note
    fork again
      :SigLIP 2 NAFlex\nMulti-Task (~50ms);
      note right
        **5 Head Groups (19 heads total):**
        IQA (sharpness, noise, contrast, exposure)
        Script (16+ scripts — refinement of Step 2)
        Orientation+Skew (verification pass)
        Handwriting (detection)
        Page Attrs (shadows, warping, paper type)

        Fallback: confidence-based classical
        fallback (6 head-specific rules)

        **Level 2 Detail:**
        model-training/prepare-doc-training-workflow-high-level.puml

        **Source:**
        - src/.../detection/iqa_ml.py
        - src/.../orchestration/device_orchestrator.py
      end note
    fork again
      :Layout Analysis\n(Docling Layout Models);
      note right
        11+ DocLayNet classes
        docling-layout-egret-xlarge (accuracy)
        docling-layout-heron (speed)
        Runs on corrected + lossless image.
        Conditional on text gate result (Step 5).

        **Source:**
        - src/.../detection/doclayout_yolo.py
        - src/.../detection/layout_lite/*.py
      end note
    end fork
  endif

  :Step 7 — Quality Corrections;
  note left
    CLAHE, sharpening, denoising.
    Applied AFTER IQA measurement so that IQA
    scores reflect original document quality.
    Guided by Classical IQA + SigLIP 2 outputs.
    Confidence-based classical fallback if
    SigLIP 2 confidence is low.

    **Source:**
    src/.../correction/corrections.py

    **Documentation:**
    docs/api/correction.md
  end note

  :Step 8 — Calculate DQS + routing;
  note right
    **Source:**
    - src/.../metrics/dqs_calculator.py
    - src/.../routing/recommendation_engine.py

    **ADR:**
    docs/ADRs/0030-document-quality-score.md

    **Level 2 Detail:**
    production-runtime/prepare-doc-primary-workflow-detailed.puml
  end note
}

:DocumentMetadata.json\n+ Corrected images;

:Handoff to Unify;
note right
  **AB Contract:**
  - Quality assessment (original quality scores)
  - Layout detection results
  - Reading order + table structure
  - Routing recommendation
  - Corrected page images (post-CLAHE)

  **Source:**
  - src/.../schema.py
  - src/.../output/json_generator.py

  **Documentation:**
  docs/api/schema.md
  docs/guides/project-b-handoff.md

  **Level 2 Detail (downstream-context/):**
  unify-ocr-layout-workflow.puml (Prepare-Doc → Unify)
  chunk-fusion-chunking-workflow.puml (Unify → Chunk)
  embed-vectorstore-workflow.puml (Chunk → Embed)
  prepare-audio-transcription-workflow.puml (Prepare-Audio track)
  data_ingestor-migration.puml (Chunk service migration)

  **Unify Focus:**
  OCR orchestration only
  (layout analysis now in Prepare-Doc)
end note

stop

